cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to the Computational Hermeneutics family or its hub, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Computational Hermeneutics: Research Tools for Computational Close Reading"
abstract: >
  The Computational Hermeneutics family landing site and map. Computational
  Hermeneutics is a family of research tools that bring the apparatus of textual
  criticism and interpretation to computational artefacts, to code as much as to
  text. The hub documents the family and links to each instrument.
